1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
Before you start your car tomorrow morning—

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,000
try this 30-second test.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
With the engine off,

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
press the brake pedal firmly and hold it.

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,500
A pedal that slowly sinks toward the floor

6
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,000
can point to fluid bypassing worn seals inside the master cylinder.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
That's an internal leak — no puddle on the ground,

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
but less stopping power when you need it most.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,500
One clue is not a diagnosis—

10
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,000
worth checking before you're back on the road.

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Stop by and we'll take a look—

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Nick's Tire and Auto, on Euclid Avenue.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
